3D Map Explainer demo · 《霍尔木兹海峡》 Strait of Hormuz · third-party data, assets and sources

## Map data and imagery (downloaded by build.sh into demo/raw/ and processed into demo/assets/; not in git)
- Elevation and bathymetry: AWS Terrain Tiles (Mapzen / Tilezen "terrarium" PNG), https://registry.opendata.aws/terrain-tiles/
  zoom 10 for the strait (tools/fetch.py), zoom 8 for the region from the Red Sea to the Gulf of Oman (tools/fetch_wide.py).
  Sources include SRTM (public domain), GMTED, ETOPO1 and GEBCO; attribution as required by the terrain-tiles documentation.
- Imagery: Sentinel-2 cloudless 2016 - https://s2maps.eu by EOX IT Services GmbH (Contains modified Copernicus Sentinel data
  2016 & 2017), CC BY 4.0. Layer s2cloudless_3857: zoom 11 (strait), zoom 9 (region; also laid over the globe), zoom 4 (whole
  globe, tools/fetch_world.py). Later Sentinel-2 cloudless releases are CC BY-NC-SA and are not used.
- Traffic separation scheme: © OpenStreetMap contributors, Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0, via the Overpass API
  (ways 220138792, 220138754 and their boundaries; raw/tss.json, raw/seamark_strait.json). The coordinates used are written
  into index.html (the IN array); the approximation between the OSM segments is described in FACTS.md.
- Oil terminal and pipeline end-point positions: public coordinates. Routes and pipeline paths are schematic.
- The film carries a credit line in the bottom-right corner throughout: data EIA · IEA, elevation AWS Terrain Tiles,
  imagery Sentinel-2 cloudless 2016 by EOX (CC BY 4.0), lanes © OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL), routes schematic,
  vertical ×3.2.
- Every download URL and date is logged in demo/raw/manifest.jsonl (kept with the local data).

## Facts
- Every number on screen and in the narration is sourced in demo/FACTS.md (EIA Today in Energy, 16 June 2025; IEA
  "Strait of Hormuz", February 2026), with URLs and quoted wording; the section depths are a measurement on the tiles above.

## Voice
- Kokoro-82M (hexgrad), voice bm_george, Apache License 2.0; run locally via kokoro-onnx (MIT) through the library's
  core/tts/tts.py. Speech check: faster-whisper base.en (MIT; OpenAI Whisper weights, MIT). Script: demo/voice/lines.json.

## Music samples (CC0; credit not required, given with thanks)
- VS Chamber Orchestra: Community Edition (Versilian Studios): contrabass (arco, pizzicato), cellos (arco, spiccato),
  violins (pizzicato), horn, timpani.
- Versilian Community Sample Library (Versilian Studios): hand chimes, bowed vibraphone, glockenspiel, harp, frame drum.
- Ambience, foley and the sine pedal are procedural (core/audio/sfx.py and demo/mix.py).

